<worksheet margin="0.5in">
    <title>Quiz: Scheduling Attempt 2</title>
  
  <introduction>
    <p>
      Name: <fillin characters="45"/>
    </p>

    <assemblage>
      <title>Scheduling Algorithms</title>
      <sidebyside widths="60% 35%" valigns="top top">
        <stack>
          <p><em>List Processing</em></p>
          <p>
            <ol>
              <li>
                <p>Mark every ready task.</p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>Give each processor the first ready task in the priority list. Mark that task as in progress so it is not assigned twice.</p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>If an available processor has no ready task, leave it idle.</p>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </p>
        </stack>
        <stack>
          <p><em>Decreasing Time</em></p>
          <p>
            <ol>
              <li>
                <p>Create a priority list by arranging tasks from longest <em>individual duration</em> to shortest.</p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>Break ties by placing the smaller task number first.</p>
              </li>
              <li>
                <p>Use that list with the list processing algorithm for the stated number of processors.</p>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </p>
        </stack>
      </sidebyside>
    </assemblage>
  </introduction>
  
  <exercise>
    <statement>
      <p>Use the decreasing-time algorithm to create a priority list for the digraph below. Then use your list to schedule the project with <em>two processors</em>.</p>
      <p>Task times are shown in blue, in parentheses. When more than one processor is available, assign tasks in processor-number order.</p>
      <image source="images/scheduling-decreasing-time.svg" width="35%">
        <shortdescription>Project digraph with 7 tasks. Task names are black and task times are blue. Arrows show prerequisites; the detailed description lists all tasks, times, and immediate prerequisites.</shortdescription>
        <description>
          <p>Each vertex shows a task name and its time in parentheses. Each arrow points from a prerequisite to the task that depends on it.</p>
          <tabular row-headers="yes" halign="left">
            <col width="15%"/>
            <col width="23%"/>
            <col width="62%"/>
            <row header="yes" bottom="minor">
              <cell>Task</cell>
              <cell>Time required</cell>
              <cell>Immediate prerequisites</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>
                <m>T_1</m>
              </cell>
              <cell>2</cell>
              <cell>None</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>
                <m>T_2</m>
              </cell>
              <cell>8</cell>
              <cell>None</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>
                <m>T_3</m>
              </cell>
              <cell>4</cell>
              <cell>None</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>
                <m>T_4</m>
              </cell>
              <cell>11</cell>
              <cell>
                <m>T_1</m>
              </cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>
                <m>T_5</m>
              </cell>
              <cell>12</cell>
              <cell>
                <m>T_1, T_2</m>
              </cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>
                <m>T_6</m>
              </cell>
              <cell>9</cell>
              <cell>
                <m>T_4, T_5</m>
              </cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>
                <m>T_7</m>
              </cell>
              <cell>10</cell>
              <cell>
                <m>T_3, T_4, T_5</m>
              </cell>
            </row>
          </tabular>
        </description>
      </image>
      <p>Write your priority list and draw or write the complete schedule. For each processor, show every task's start and finish times and include all idle intervals. State the project's completion time.</p>
      <image source="images/schedule-two-processors.png" width="80%">
        <shortdescription>
          Blank schedule for two processors from time 0 to 40.
          Dashed lines mark each time unit, and heavier solid lines
          mark every five time units.
        </shortdescription>
      </image>
    </statement>
  </exercise>

  <exercise>
    <statement>
      <p>Use the list-processing algorithm to schedule the project below with <em>three processors</em> and the following priority list:</p>
      <me>T_8, T_4, T_3, T_{10}, T_5, T_7, T_1, T_9, T_6, T_2</me>
      <p>Task times are shown in blue, in parentheses. When more than one processor is available, assign tasks in processor-number order.</p>
      <image source="images/scheduling-priority-three-processors.svg" width="50%">
        <shortdescription>Project digraph with 10 tasks. Task names are black and task times are blue. Arrows show prerequisites; the detailed description lists all tasks, times, and immediate prerequisites.</shortdescription>
        <description>
          <p>Each vertex shows a task name and its time in parentheses. Each arrow points from a prerequisite to the task that depends on it.</p>
          <tabular row-headers="yes" halign="left">
            <col width="15%"/>
            <col width="23%"/>
            <col width="62%"/>
            <row header="yes" bottom="minor">
              <cell>Task</cell>
              <cell>Time required</cell>
              <cell>Immediate prerequisites</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>
                <m>T_1</m>
              </cell>
              <cell>7</cell>
              <cell>None</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>
                <m>T_2</m>
              </cell>
              <cell>4</cell>
              <cell>None</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>
                <m>T_3</m>
              </cell>
              <cell>12</cell>
              <cell>None</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>
                <m>T_4</m>
              </cell>
              <cell>5</cell>
              <cell>None</cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>
                <m>T_5</m>
              </cell>
              <cell>3</cell>
              <cell>
                <m>T_1, T_2</m>
              </cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>
                <m>T_6</m>
              </cell>
              <cell>2</cell>
              <cell>
                <m>T_2</m>
              </cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>
                <m>T_7</m>
              </cell>
              <cell>8</cell>
              <cell>
                <m>T_3</m>
              </cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>
                <m>T_8</m>
              </cell>
              <cell>9</cell>
              <cell>
                <m>T_6, T_7</m>
              </cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>
                <m>T_9</m>
              </cell>
              <cell>10</cell>
              <cell>
                <m>T_5</m>
              </cell>
            </row>
            <row>
              <cell>
                <m>T_{10}</m>
              </cell>
              <cell>6</cell>
              <cell>
                <m>T_5, T_8</m>
              </cell>
            </row>
          </tabular>
        </description>
      </image>
      <p>Draw or write the complete schedule. For each processor, show every task's start and finish times and include all idle intervals. State the project's completion time.</p>
      <image source="images/schedule-three-processors.png" width="80%">
        <shortdescription>
          Blank schedule for three processors from time 0 to 40.
          Dashed lines mark each time unit, and heavier solid lines
          mark every five time units.
        </shortdescription>
      </image>
    </statement>
  </exercise>
</worksheet>
